WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.368 --> 00:00:11.808
On the wedding morning, makeup and hair for the wedding parents have to be finished within a set time before heading to the wedding hall.

2
00:00:12.144 --> 00:00:24.432
So both the artist and the client are often rushed, and every so often we sadly see reviews mentioning how upsetting it was when the hairstyle came loose partway through.

3
00:00:24.768 --> 00:00:28.560
Here's what to do if that happens.

4
00:00:28.896 --> 00:00:39.000
Wedding parents are often so absorbed in greeting guests and the event itself that they don't notice their hair has come loose — usually someone nearby spots it and lets them know.

5
00:00:39.336 --> 00:00:48.648
Don't panic — just pull one or two pins from a spot where it won't show and use them to secure the loose section.

6
00:00:48.984 --> 00:00:59.184
No special technique is usually needed — most of the time it's just weak hold, so re-pinning it is the best fix.

7
00:00:59.520 --> 00:01:07.368
That said, the ends of pins are often bent to keep them in place, so be careful when pulling them out.

8
00:01:07.704 --> 00:01:11.088
Ease them out slowly and carefully.

9
00:01:11.424 --> 00:01:17.712
That way you can secure the loose hair without messing it up further.

10
00:01:18.048 --> 00:01:29.208
Setting it firmly with pins and spray from the start is the best way to prevent this altogether, but if hair does come loose on rare occasions, this is how to fix it.
